{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q135682603","formula":"C₂₃H₂₉N₃O","hill":"C23H29N3O","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":23.0,"H":29.0,"N":3.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"MAL-LAD"},"descriptions":{"en":"MAL-LAD, or MALLAD, also known as METAL-LAD or METALLAD, as well as 6-methallyl-6-nor-LSD, is a serotonin receptor modulator of the lysergamide family related to lysergic acid diethylamide (LSD). The drug acts as a non-selective serotonin receptor agonist, including of the serotonin 5-HT2A receptor among others. It is also a dopamine receptor agonist, though unlike other lysergamides, does not show activity at the dopamine D1 and D5 receptors."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":"C=C(C)CN1C[C@H](C(=O)N(CC)CC)C=C2c3cccc4[nH]cc(c34)C[C@H]21","inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":null,"atoms":56,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.084,"y":4.443,"z":-2.286,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.679,"y":3.827,"z":-1.25,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.676,"y":4.427,"z":0.128,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.414,"y":2.511,"z":-1.413,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.873,"y":1.445,"z":-0.55,"el":"N"},{"x":0.442,"y":1.001,"z":-1.072,"el":"C"},{"x":1.12,"y":0.011,"z":-0.105,"el":"C"},{"x":2.423,"y":-0.516,"z":-0.733,"el":"C"},{"x":2.553,"y":-0.577,"z":-1.96,"el":"O"},{"x":3.436,"y":-0.967,"z":0.122,"el":"N"},{"x":4.667,"y":-1.467,"z":-0.496,"el":"C"},{"x":5.599,"y":-0.359,"z":-0.964,"el":"C"},{"x":3.413,"y":-0.842,"z":1.583,"el":"C"},{"x":3.948,"y":0.494,"z":2.074,"el":"C"},{"x":0.198,"y":-1.144,"z":0.191,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.13,"y":-1.044,"z":-0.002,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.025,"y":-2.193,"z":0.265,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.729,"y":-3.56,"z":0.229,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.72,"y":-4.511,"z":0.511,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.035,"y":-4.138,"z":0.836,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.314,"y":-2.77,"z":0.